  "source": "BeagleBone Black System Reference Manual, board and cape dimension figures, and the Rev C assembly drawing (github.com/beagleboard/beaglebone-black): board 3.40 x 2.15 inch (86.36 x 54.61 mm) with 0.25 inch corners at the Ethernet end and 0.5 inch corners at the far end, four 0.125 inch holes at (0.575, 0.125), (0.575, 2.025), (3.175, 0.25) and (3.175, 1.90) inch. P8 and P9 are 2 x 23 sockets starting 0.8 inch from the Ethernet end. The Ethernet jack, USB host socket, mini USB, micro HDMI, processor, eMMC, buttons and serial header are placed from the assembly drawing outlines; the DC jack and the microSD slot are placed from their reference labels and are approximate.",
